ntract and brief\\\"\\n6:   - \\\"phase 5 recommendation contract and brief\\\"\\n7: importance_tier: \\\"normal\\\"\\n8: contextType: \\\"general\\\"\\n9: ---\\n10: <!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core | v2.4 -->\\n11: # Feature Specification: Phase 5: recommendation-contract-and-brief\\n12: \\n13: <!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\\n14: ---\\n15: \\n16: <!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\\n17: ## 1. METADATA\\n18: \\n19: | Field | Value |\\n20: |-------|-------|\\n21: | **Level** | 2 |\\n22: | **Priority** | P1 |\\n23: | **Status** | Draft |\\n24: | **Created** | 2026-11-12 |\\n25: | **Branch** | `worktrees/352-command-surfacing-research` |\\n26: | **Parent Spec** | ../spec.md |\\n27: | **Phase** | 5 of 7 |\\n28: | **Predecessor** | 004-command-meaning-matching |\\n29: | **Success...","title":"grep","metadata":{"metadata":{"matches":23,"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Found 23 matches\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/acceptance-criteria.md:\n  Line 71: | AC-019 | REQ-019 | Given a re-capture after the source fix, When row `nm-sk-doc-01` is scored, Then its top is `sk-doc` with no command, the diff holds no two-word window of its prompt, and typed recall, plain recall, false offers and the four pinned numbers are not lower | `jq -c '.rows[\"nm-sk-doc-01\"] \\| {top, offered}'` on the baseline file prints `{\"top\":\"sk-doc\",\"offered\":false}`, the T056 window check prints nothing, and the T057 `M` and `P` outputs | Unmet | - |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/goal.md:\n  Line 62: - [ ] The corpus row `nm-sk-doc-01` has `sk-doc` as its top in `command-routing-baseline.json`.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/tasks.md:\n  Line 70: - [ ] T054 Write `$S/nm-sk-doc-probe.mjs`, which sets `VITEST`, imports `scoreAdvisorPrompt` from `$ADV/dist/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.js` and prints, for `sk-doc`, `system-skilled-doctor`, `sk-code` and `sk-design`, the confidence, the score and each positive lane contribution with its evidence, for the prompt of row `nm-sk-doc-01`. Save the output (`$S/nm-sk-doc-before.txt`). Verify: the output matches the probe block in `spec.md`, with `sk-doc` absent and `sk-code` holding `token:typo` and `token:heading`.\n\n  Line 131: - [ ] T056 Make one correction at the source T055 names: remove a token a skill holds only through a harvest artifact, or add a general documentation-edit term to the `sk-doc` source field T055 names. The change adds no string of two or more consecutive words from the `nm-sk-doc-01` prompt. When the file is a deriver input, run `node $D`. Verify: for each two-word window of the prompt, `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff HEAD -U0 -- <changed file> | rg -F \"<window>\"` prints nothing, `node $D --check | jq -r .status` prints `fresh`, and after `npm run build` in `ADV`, `node $S/nm-sk-doc-probe.mjs` prints `sk-doc` with the highest score.\n\n  Line 134: - [ ] T057 Run `npm run build` in `ADV`, then `node $C --write`. Verify: `jq -c '.rows[\"nm-sk-doc-01\"] | {top, offered}' $ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json` prints `{\"top\":\"sk-doc\",\"offered\":false}`, `node $C | $M` prints typed at least 24 of 44, tune combined at least 9 of 45, holdout combined at least 0 of 44 and false offers 0 of 35, and `$P` prints numbers no lower than `[159,50,20]` with false fire no higher than 5. If any is worse, revert T056 and mark it `[B]` with the printed numbers.\n\n  Line 231: - [ ] CHK-024 [P1] `nm-sk-doc-01` tops at `sk-doc` with no recall or pinned number lower (T057).\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/spec.md:\n  Line 153: The near-miss row `nm-sk-doc-01` sits in split `none`, so its prompt may be read. The probe below imports the built scorer with `VITEST` set, as the capture does, and prints each named skill's positive lane contributions. It ran from the repository root on the same commit. The output is verbatim.\n\n  Line 156: $ jq -c '.rows[\"nm-sk-doc-01\"]' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json\n\n  Line 202: - Make `nm-sk-doc-01` route to `sk-doc` by correcting the routing signal at its source, never by a phrase copied from its prompt.\n\n  Line 234: | The one routing source file the `nm-sk-doc-01` trace names | Modify | One signal corrected at its source |\n\n  Line 270: | REQ-019 | The near-miss row `nm-sk-doc-01` (`fix the typo in the heading of the setup guide`, split `none`) has top `sk-doc` and no command after a re-capture. The fix corrects the routing signal at its source and adds no string of two or more consecutive words from that prompt. Typed recall, tune and holdout plain recall, false offers and the four pinned numbers are not lower. |\n\n  Line 303: | Risk | The `nm-sk-doc-01` fix moves other rows | Med: a correction to a shared token changes other prompts | The four pinned numbers, typed and plain recall and false offers must not be lower after the re-capture |\n\n  Line 366: - Is the `nm-sk-doc-01` miss fixed here? Decision: \"Fix it in phase 005 (Recommended)\". It is REQ-019.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/plan.md:\n  Line 107: Setup records the before numbers, the live brief heads, the reach check, the hook timing and the suite. Implementation waits for the phase 007 confirmation, then runs the waves in `tasks.md`: the table, the fields, the head, the degraded contract, the reach check, the tests, the id retirement, the `nm-sk-doc-01` fix and the CARRY-003 group. Verification rebuilds, reruns every floor, the CLI checks, the brief heads, the reach check with real embeddings and the suite, then fills the summary.\n\n  Line 134: | The `nm-sk-doc-01` source trace | Internal | Open: the token sources are UNKNOWN until T055 | The fix task T056 cannot name its file |\n\n  Line 172: The operator answered the four design questions on 2026-11-12, each with the recommended option: \"Rename the four, drop /prompt (Recommended)\", \"Only a typed command (Recommended)\", \"The strictest: ask (Recommended)\" and \"No (Recommended)\". The same day the operator kept CARRY-003 in this phase, moved the `nm-sk-doc-01` fix here (\"Fix it in phase 005 (Recommended)\") and set phase 007's before-measurement first (\"Now, on today's branch tip (Recommended)\"). `spec.md` section 10 holds each answer.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/implementation-summary.md:\n  Line 77: | Operator answers of 2026-11-12 | All four design questions took the recommended option. CARRY-003 stays, and the `nm-sk-doc-01` fix moved here. `spec.md` section 10 quotes each answer |\n\n  Line 96: 1. **The `nm-sk-doc-01` fix names no file yet.** Which source projects `typo` and `heading` onto `sk-code` is UNKNOWN until task T055 traces it, so task T056 picks its file from that trace.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/scratch/logs/w0a-T004.out:\n  Line 3: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1794521815885,\"sessionID\":\"ses_e2e2a8545ffel5iCm3sO3VeatJ\",\"part\":{\"par