{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794521847910,"sessionID":"ses_e2e2a7dd5ffeKSW8P83xK0M1au","part":{"partID":"prt_1d1d6558a001gQFMm3anhNqFf9","sessionID":"ses_e2e2a7dd5ffeKSW8P83xK0M1au","messageID":"msg_1d1d645a3001GNeacWs01WdAcU","type":"tool","id":"call_32768533576a4fa2987cdf47","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/spec.md","offset":130,"limit":90},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/spec.md, lines 130-219\n130: {\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}\n131: {\"tune\":{\"own\":2,\"attached\":7,\"combined\":9,\"total\":45},\"holdout\":{\"own\":0,\"attached\":0,\"combined\":0,\"total\":44}}\n132: {\"count\":0,\"total\":35}\n133: [\"cmd-create-agent-typed-01\"]\n134: ```\n135: \n136: The holdout count above is a line count only. No holdout prompt text was read.\n137: \n138: The reach check below ran from the repository root on the same commit with Ollama serving `nomic-embed-text:v1.5`, so command rows score on meaning. It exited 1. The output is the last eight lines, verbatim.\n139: \n140: ```text\n141: $ node .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/ci-router-vocabulary-reach.cjs --hub sk-doc\n142: FAIL sk-doc                       declared=257 wrong-hub=  0 outranked=  4 no-reach=  0 allowed=  6 probe-error=  0 operator-local=  0\n143:        outranked  create an agent                            create:agent=0.8200, sk-doc=0.8265\n144:        outranked  opencode agent                             create:agent=0.8000, sk-code=0.9069\n145:        outranked  deterministic scenario                     create:manual-testing-playbook=0.8000, sk-doc=0.8329\n146:        outranked  manual test scenario                       create:manual-testing-playbook=0.8200, sk-doc=0.9204\n147: \n148: checked=1 hub(s), wrong-hub=0, outranked=4, no-reach=0, allowed=6, probe-error=0, operator-local=0\n149: advisor generation: 83\n150: RESULT: FAILED\n151: ```\n152: \n153: The near-miss row `nm-sk-doc-01` sits in split `none`, so its prompt may be read. The probe below imports the built scorer with `VITEST` set, as the capture does, and prints each named skill's positive lane contributions. It ran from the repository root on the same commit. The output is verbatim.\n154: \n155: ```text\n156: $ jq -c '.rows[\"nm-sk-doc-01\"]' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json\n157: {\"expected_command\":null,\"top\":\"system-skilled-doctor\",\"top1\":false,\"top3\":false,\"offered\":false}\n158: $ node <scratchpad>/nm-probe.mjs .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/dist/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.js . \"fix the typo in the heading of the setup guide\"\n159: system-skilled-doctor 0.82 0.1302 [[\"lexical\",0.056,[\"token:setup\"]],[\"derived_generated\",0.0662,[\"derived:setup\"]],[\"semantic_shadow\",0.008,[\"shadow:test-fallback\"]]]\n160: sk-code 0.82 0.0969 [[\"lexical\",0.0812,[\"token:typo\",\"token:heading\",\"token:debug\"]],[\"graph_causal\",0.0157,[\"edge:mcp-tooling->sk-code:enhances\",\"edge:sk-design->sk-code:enhances\"]]]\n161: sk-design 0.82 0.0640 [[\"lexical\",0.056,[\"token:guide\"]],[\"semantic_shadow\",0.008,[\"shadow:test-fallback\"]]]\n162: count 4 skdoc index -1\n163: ```\n164: \n165: `sk-doc` is not among the scored rows at all, and `sk-code` holds `typo` and `heading`. Which source file and field projects each of those tokens is UNKNOWN until the trace in `tasks.md` runs. A plain `rg -w \"typo|heading\"` over the four skills' `ROUTER.md`, `SKILL.md`, `hub-router.json` and `graph-metadata.json` printed nothing.\n166: \n167: In each of the four rows the winner is a command row that `sk-doc` owns. `rankShippedFleet` in that script counts a hit only when the first shipped `skillId` equals the probed hub, and the public recommendation carries no owner it could read instead.\n168: \n169: ### What Already Exists\n170: Each part was read in the code on 2026-11-12. `ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`.\n171: - An optional `command` field on `AdvisorRecommendationSchema` (`ADV/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`), set only when a hub attaches a mode command through `attachCommand` (`ADV/lib/command-attach.ts`) in `enrichCompiledRoutes` (`ADV/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`).\n172: - The schema object is `.strict()`, so an unknown fifth field is already rejected.\n173: - `kind` exists on the scored recommendation (`ScoredRecommendation.kind` in `ADV/lib/scorer/types.ts`) and `publicRecommendation` drops it.\n174: - A hub never repeats a command whose own row ranks in the same result (`BRIDGE_COMMAND_BY_ID` and `alreadyOffered` in `enrichCompiledRoutes`). The option `compiledRouteTopOnly` exists. Neither is planned again.\n175: - The CLI hook path keeps `command` (`recommendationFromCli` in `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts`) and retries once without a rejected option for an older daemon (`invokeAdvisorRecommendPayload` and `COMPILED_ROUTE_OPTION_KEYS` in `ADV/skill-advisor-cli.ts`).\n176: - The doctor runnable string with its route target, such as `/doctor:git hooks`, is generated into `DOCTOR_COMMAND_STRINGS` (`ADV/lib/render.ts`) by `renderDoctorCommandStrings` (`ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs`). That covers the L6 runnable string for doctor rows.\n177: - One policy per command and per doctor route is generated as `commandPolicies` by `derivePolicy` and `commandPolicies` in the deriver.\n178: - The TypeScript hand-authored array is gone from `ADV/lib/scorer/projection.ts`, and all 62 generated rows set `routingEnabled` (45 true, 17 false).\n179: - The allow-list holds 4 rows, not 8. `/spec_kit`, `/memory:save`, `/prompt` and the umbrella `command-spec-kit` have no allow-list row, and `AGENTS.md` names none of the retired ids.\n180: - No two TypeScript-enabled rows share a runnable string (counted from the generated file).\n181: \n182: ### What Is Missing\n183: - `kind`, `policy` and `ownerSkillId` on the public recommendation, and `command` on a command row's own entry.\n184: - A brief label for any non-doctor command row and any attached command. Today the head prints the raw id or the hub skill alone.\n185: - A policy for `/doctor:update`, whose bridge names no action while its six actions carry three different policies.\n186: - A stated contract for a degraded result. The local Python scorer returns `command-create-readme` as a passing row for a plain prompt.\n187: - The four allow-list ids, the Python `\"/prompt\"` lexical row and owner branch, the two Python hand-authored constants and the optional `routingEnabled` type.\n188: - An owner-aware hit in the router vocabulary reach check. Without it the check fails on `sk-doc` with real embeddings on, because a meaning-passed command that `sk-doc` owns ranks first.\n189: <!-- /ANCHOR:measured-behavior -->\n190: \n191: ---\n192: \n193: <!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n194: ## 3. SCOPE\n195: \n196: ### In Scope\n197: - Generate one table `COMMAND_ROWS` in `ADV/lib/command-attach.ts`, keyed by every id a scorer can return for a command entry, holding its runnable `command`, `policy` and `ownerSkillId`, plus `COMMAND_POLICIES` keyed by runnable string. It replaces the doctor-only `DOCTOR_COMMAND_STRINGS`.\n198: - Add `kind`, `policy` and `ownerSkillId` to the public recommendation and fill all four fields from that table in the handler, the CLI fallback and the renderer.\n199: - Render the brief head as `use <owner> → <command> (<policy>)` for a recommendation that names a command, with no consequence line (L12).\n200: - State and test the degraded contract on the CLI's `degraded: true` path.\n201: - Retire the allow-list file, its four ids and the Python `/prompt` residue, delete the Python hand-authored constants and make `routingEnabled` required (L7).\n202: - Make `nm-sk-doc-01` route to `sk-doc` by correcting the routing signal at its source, never by a phrase copied from its prompt.\n203: - Make `rankShippedFleet` in `ci-router-vocabulary-reach.cjs` count a winning command row whose `ownerSkillId` is the probed hub as a hit.\n204: - CARRY-003: clear the typed `/create:agent` ambiguity, prove that a metadata command with no compatibility row is active and reach `/speckit:search` from the review's probe prompt.\n205: \n206: ### Out of Scope\n207: - Raising the brief token cap. The research eliminated it, and the new head fits 80 tokens.\n208: - A consequence line or argument state in the brief (L6, L12). The command's own setup asks for its arguments.\n209: - An `argumentHint` field. No current caller reads it, and the operator answered no.\n210: - Changing a policy, a risk class or a scoring weight. Phase 002 owns the policies, and the four pinned numbers are a floor.\n211: - The `Also:` companion line. It keeps its doctor-only trigger and its runnable label.\n212: - `AGENTS.md`, the Gate 2 sentence and the runtime pointers. Phase 006 owns them.\n213: - The Python-only ids `command-spec-kit-deep-research` and `command-spec-kit-deep-review`, the TypeScript compatibility ids `create:agent` and `create:manual-testing-playbook`, and the alias folds that map old ids onto live ones. The operator chose to rename only the four allow-list ids.\n214: - Typed `/memory:save` as prompt vocabulary in `explicit.ts`, `fusion.ts`, the Python scorer and the Gate 3 classifier. It matches what a user types, and five labelled corpus rows type it.\n215: \n216: ### Files to Change\n217: \n218: | File Path | Change Type | Description |\n219: |-----------|-------------|-------------|\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 220]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"cont