tive and reach `/speckit:search` from the review's probe prompt.\n205: \n206: ### Out of Scope\n207: - Raising the brief token cap. The research eliminated it, and the new head fits 80 tokens.\n208: - A consequence line or argument state in the brief (L6, L12). The command's own setup asks for its arguments.\n209: - An `argumentHint` field. No current caller reads it, and the operator answered no.\n210: - Changing a policy, a risk class or a scoring weight. Phase 002 owns the policies, and the four pinned numbers are a floor.\n211: - The `Also:` companion line. It keeps its doctor-only trigger and its runnable label.\n212: - `AGENTS.md`, the Gate 2 sentence and the runtime pointers. Phase 006 owns them.\n213: - The Python-only ids `command-spec-kit-deep-research` and `command-spec-kit-deep-review`, the TypeScript compatibility ids `create:agent` and `create:manual-testing-playbook`, and the alias folds that map old ids onto live ones. The operator chose to rename only the four allow-list ids.\n214: - Typed `/memory:save` as prompt vocabulary in `explicit.ts`, `fusion.ts`, the Python scorer and the Gate 3 classifier. It matches what a user types, and five labelled corpus rows type it.\n215: \n216: ### Files to Change\n217: \n218: | File Path | Change Type | Description |\n219: |-----------|-------------|-------------|\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 220]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/spec.md\",\"offset\":130,\"limit\":90}"},"time":{"start":1794521847178,"end":1794521847910}}}}
